## Git operations

- Run Git commands from the current repository.
- Do not target other repositories using `git -C`,
  `--git-dir`, or `--work-tree`.
- If `git add` or `git commit` fails because the
  sandbox prevents writing to `.git`, retry only
  that command with escalated permissions.
- Keep the workspace sandbox enabled.
- Do not escalate unrelated commands.
- Do not push, amend, reset, or rebase unless
  explicitly requested.

## yomiyasu skill

- Do not use the `yomiyasu` skill to polish Japanese text while carrying out a
  user's request or writing progress updates.
- Use it only when writing the final response after the requested work is done,
  or when creating a plan file. For either case, read and follow
  `~/.agents/skills/yomiyasu/SKILL.md`; if it is missing, look for an available
  skill named `yomiyasu`.
- Preserve the user's meaning and requirements when applying the skill.

## Herdr orchestration

- At the start of a Herdr session verified by the session hook, read the
  chief-of-agents and herdr-orchestration skills. In herdr-tui, also read the
  herdr skill.
- A manually started Herdr agent session is Chief when the session hook verifies
  its Herdr identity and it is not an enrolled worker. Enroll a task with
  `agent-orchestration init` after its requirements and acceptance are known;
  do not start workers before enrollment.
- Outside a verified Herdr session, do not assume the Chief role.
